# centralize_events_lobby_smoke_udp — client 1 (slot 0).
# DS runs with the lobby state machine live. The headless's
# cmd-stdin pump falls back to a per-iteration counter while
# serverTick is still 0 (no PACKET_GAME_STATE yet), so these
# lobby ops fire on wall-clock cadence (~1ms per pump tick).
#
# Sequencing matters: c2 joins ~300ms after c1 and needs time
# to complete its UDP join + map download before its own cmd
# stream can ready it up. So c1 sets its team early but holds
# off on ready until well after c2 has had a chance to set
# team and ready. That way c1's ready is the trigger that
# tips serverSimLobbyCheckAllReady over and starts countdown
# — not c1 readying alone before c2 has joined.
{"tick": 100,  "op": "set_team",  "slot": 0, "team": 1}
{"tick": 4000, "op": "set_ready", "slot": 0, "ready": true}
